Wait, `inspect.unwrap` already does a loop for `__wrapped__`.

So:
```python
    @cached_property
    def _unwrapped_call(self) -> Any:
        if self.call is None:
            return self.call  # pragma: no cover

        call = self.call
        while hasattr(call, "func"):
            call = call.func
        return inspect.unwrap(call)
```
This will unwrap all `partial` layers, and then unwrap all `__wrapped__` layers.
Is it possible to have `partial(wrapped_func)`? Yes.
Is it possible to have `wrapped(partial_func)`? Yes.

If we have `wrapped(partial(f))`, `inspect.unwrap` will get to the `partial` object, then we stop.
If we have `partial(wrapped(f))`, `while hasattr(call, "func")` will get to the `wrapped` object, then `inspect.unwrap` will get to `f`.

So if they are interleaved, we need a loop.

```python
